      "description": "Watch West Brom vs Charlton Athletic highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 2, 2026. The Championship clash between West Bromwich Albion and Charlton Athletic delivered a tactical battle that kept spectators guessing until the final whistle. Both sides showcased resilience in a game defined by narrow margins and clinical finishing. A Strategic Stalemate in the First Half Taking place on September 2, 2026 , the match began with both teams prioritizing defensive stability. West Brom attempted to dictate the tempo through midfield possession, but Charlton Athletic remained disciplined, snuffing out potential openings before they could develop into genuine threats. The first half concluded without a breakthrough, as both managers headed to the dressing rooms looking for a way to unlock their opponent's sturdy backline. Second Half Breakthroughs The intensity rose significantly after the restart. In the 59th minute, the deadlock was finally broken when Callum Styles found the back of the net, clinical finishing giving West Brom a hard-earned lead. The goal sparked a flurry of activity on the touchline, with both teams making multiple substitutions to alter the tactical landscape. Joe Rankin-Costello and Timothy Noor Ouma were among those introduced as the managers looked to manage the shifting momentum. However, the home side's celebrations were short-lived. In the 69th minute, Tyreece Campbell delivered a composed finish to bring Charlton level. The equalizer shifted the psychological advantage back to the visitors, setting up a grandstand finish as the game entered its final twenty minutes with everything to play for. Late Drama and Disciplined Finishes As the clock ticked down, the match became increasingly physical. Tyler Bindon picked up a yellow card for Charlton in the 77th minute, followed by a series of defensive reinforcements from both camps. Late substitutes like Barney Stewart and Sonny Carey were brought on to see out the result. In stoppage time, West Brom's Isaac Price received a yellow card as the pressure mounted. Ultimately, neither side could find a decisive late winner, and the referee blew the whistle on a competitive 1-1 draw."
